Submaps looks like a good explanation. Note you cannot teleport into
the fake wizard's tower, either (with or without the portal, even if
dug out). It seems you cannot self-teleport into any area level
teleport or branchport would not place you.

However, teleporting monsters around is not prone to these
restrictions. For example, you can levitate over the moat right next
to the castle corner towers and whistle your pet(s) in. (This makes
sense with vampire lords if you give them a cloak to cancel the lichs'
touch attack.) More astonishingly, if your pet purple worm swallows
you due to conflict and you then take the ring off, you stay swallowed
even if you whistle it around. You can travel on non-teleport levels
this way, tested on the wizard quest home. (Displace it to get back
out).

People who want to test non-teleport level restrictions should
probably prepare a wizard mode bones file, and make sure it doesn't
get into hearse.


